"comparison": "Both AVGO and AMD describe core offerings to modernize and manage enterprise IT infrastructure, but they focus on different layers of the stack. AVGO focuses on the software and networking fabric layer, stating its software 'help enterprises simplify their information technology (\"IT\") environments' and 'manage... hybrid cloud environments,' while also offering 'fibre channel storage area networking (\"FC SAN\") products.' In contrast, AMD focuses on the underlying silicon compute layer, offering 'data center computing solutions including AI accelerators, microprocessors (CPUs), graphic processing units (GPUs)... to meet the vast computing performance requirements of today's data centers... and cloud environments.' AVGO provides the integration and management layer for the environment, whereas AMD provides the high-performance processing engines within that environment.",
